<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guillermo Endara</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936–2009</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guillermo Endara was a Panamanian lawyer and politician who won the presidential election of May 1989 as the opposition candidate, only for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-noriega">Manuel Noriega</a> to annul the result. He was sworn in on a US military base as American forces invaded in December 1989 and served as president until 1994. His government dismantled the military, rebuilt democratic institutions and handed power to an elected successor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guillermo-endara.jpg" alt="Guillermo Endara" width="294" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: White House Photo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guillermo_Endara_1993.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
